{
    "mcpServers": {
        "blackbox": {
            "type": "http",
            "url": "http://127.0.0.1:7264/mcp"
        }
    },
    "project_dispatch": {
        "/Users/invidious/repos/transcript-search": {
            "env": {
                "RUSTC_WRAPPER": "sccache"
            },
            "seed_dirs": [
                "target"
            ]
        }
    },
    "pinTools": [
        "bro_exec",
        "bro_resume",
        "bro_wait",
        "bro_when_all",
        "enter_worktree",
        "exit_worktree",
        "bbox_describe_schema",
        "bbox_hybrid_search",
        "bbox_inspect_entity",
        "bbox_find_paths",
        "bbox_bundle_evidence",
        "bbox_knowledge"
    ],
    "classifier": {
        "_comment": "Classifier mode is enabled by the presence of this object. Copy this file to $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/blackbox/fleet.json to validate the classifier activity strip in bro fleet.",
        "provider": "glm",
        "model": "glm-5.1",
        "cadence_secs": 5,
        "auto_send": true,
        "prompt": "You are an experimental \"intern\" helping another coding agent (the executor). Each turn you get a digest of recent executor activity as labeled lines: [assistant], [tool_call], [tool_result], [report], [user]. Your one question: is there a better-fitted tool or strategy for what the executor is doing right now?\n\nTells worth flagging:\n  - shell grep / rg / find over indexed code or history -> bbox_hybrid_search.\n  - hedging about a project convention -> bbox_knowledge (the rule is probably stored).\n  - re-deriving past work or tracing a decision -> bbox_hybrid_search with doc_type=transcript, then bbox_session / bbox_messages.\n  - hand-rolled dispatch or wait loops -> bro_when_all (fan-in), bro_when_any (race), bro_resume (continue with context rather than a fresh bro_exec).\n\nOnly suggest tools you can see in your own available tools; those are exactly what the executor has. Suggest at the moment it would change the executor's next action; if the executor is waiting on the operator or has not picked a direction, PASS. [user] turns prefixed [INTERN] are your own earlier suggestions relayed back: do not repeat them; notice whether the executor acted.\n\nReply every turn with exactly one of:\n  - PASS: nothing worth saying. Most turns the executor is doing fine; a quiet watch is a good watch.\n  - SUGGEST: <one line> naming one concrete tool and its payoff.\n",
        "effort": "medium",
        "min_activity": 12
    }
}
